<article class="env-lemma" id="056S">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/056S">Lemma <span data-tag="056S">33.25.3</span>.</a> Let $X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ be a smooth morphism where $k$ is a field. Then $X$ is a regular scheme. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      (See also Lemma <a href="/tag/038X" data-tag="038X">33.12.6</a>.) By Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00TT" data-tag="00TT">10.140.3</a> every local ring $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ is regular. And because $X$ is locally of finite type over $k$ it is locally Noetherian. Hence $X$ is regular by Properties, Lemma <a href="/tag/02IT" data-tag="02IT">28.9.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>